            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I believe that the only piece of code depending on `Comment.nvim` here is the [`get_cstring()`](https://github.com/L3MON4D3/LuaSnip/wiki/Cool-Snippets#finding-the-comment-string) function? If yes, does the following snippet work for you?\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal get_cstring = function()\r\n  local left, right = unpack(vim.fn.split(vim.bo.commentstring, '%s'))\r\n  return { left or '', right or '' }\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe 'mini.comment' module works only with whole line commenting, so no need to do anything with block comments.",
