        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> @echasnovski I'm not sure if it is expected behavior,\r\n\r\nIt says that `get_cstring()` doesn't expect arguments, which is true, because it works only for line commenting. No need for `opts.ctype`.\r\n\r\n> Also this doesn't seem to work with treesitter commentstring, ex, I set nix ft comment to \"# %s\", but Luasnip automatically insert /* %s*/. Hope you might have better solution. \r\n\r\nIt uses `vim.bo.commentstring` to compute parts. Make sure it is set to an appropriate one.\r\n\r\nIf you use 'JoosepAlviste/nvim-ts-context-commentstring', then make sure to execute `require(\"ts_context_commentstring.internal\").update_commentstring({})` prior. Maybe something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal get_cstring = function()\r\n  require(\"ts_context_commentstring.internal\").update_commentstring({})\r\n  local left, right = unpack(vim.fn.split(vim.bo.commentstring, '%s'))\r\n  return { left or '', right or '' }\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\n> I will reopen the issue, but feel free to close it if you think it's not worth it. Many thanks for your time and effort!\r\n\r\nYes, I think I am going to close this, as it really has nothing to do with 'mini.comment'.",
